WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.293
The Times told

00:00:01.105 --> 00:00:02.024
photographers

00:00:02.107 --> 00:00:03.262
skip the Photoshop

00:00:03.074 --> 00:00:03.710
update

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:04.937
The New York

00:00:04.749 --> 00:00:05.845
Times is asking

00:00:05.657 --> 00:00:07.071
freelance photographers

00:00:06.883 --> 00:00:07.826
not to install

00:00:07.638 --> 00:00:09.395
Photoshop 2027

00:00:09.572 --> 00:00:10.479
because its new

00:00:10.291 --> 00:00:11.505
AI features work

00:00:11.317 --> 00:00:12.130
in ways that

00:00:11.942 --> 00:00:12.626
may not be

00:00:12.438 --> 00:00:13.628
apparent to users

00:00:14.158 --> 00:00:15.018
The worry is

00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:15.667
metadata

00:00:15.806 --> 00:00:16.690
The update can

00:00:16.502 --> 00:00:17.704
tag photos as

00:00:17.516 --> 00:00:18.553
AI-generated

00:00:18.813 --> 00:00:19.921
even after routine

00:00:19.733 --> 00:00:20.263
edits

00:00:20.311 --> 00:00:20.983
and for a

00:00:20.794 --> 00:00:22.056
newsroom that keeps

00:00:21.903 --> 00:00:22.834
editing minimal

00:00:22.893 --> 00:00:24.155
that risks readers'

00:00:23.966 --> 00:00:24.697
trust

00:00:25.238 --> 00:00:26.830
Adobe's November update

00:00:26.665 --> 00:00:27.655
adds an AI

00:00:27.467 --> 00:00:28.669
Assisted Editor view

00:00:28.894 --> 00:00:30.120
an editing assistant

00:00:30.226 --> 00:00:31.806
prompt-based transforms

00:00:31.854 --> 00:00:33.197
new upscaling and

00:00:33.009 --> 00:00:33.834
a tool that

00:00:33.658 --> 00:00:35.273
recomposes images for

00:00:35.085 --> 00:00:36.488
different canvas sizes

00:00:37.014 --> 00:00:38.028
Full story on

00:00:37.839 --> 00:00:38.735
the dashboard
